        "commit_message": "There were several large spikes due to tests that spawn worker processes.\nHere's what locally helped me to cut down on peak memory usage:\n- Make `cythonize` use serial builds on GraalPy by default.\n`ProcessPoolExecutor` creates a process per CPU core, which is excessive\non GraalPy. We patch `multiprocessing.Pool` to lower the default number\nof processes if you pass `None`, but we missed that\n`ProcessPoolExecutor` has its own code for this so it's still using CPU\ncore count.\n- Reduce the parallelism on GraalPy used by `common_include_dir` test.\nThere other tests that still have parallelism, but those didn't show up\nin my investigation, so I'm keeping this minimal for now.\n\nI haven't found any memory leaks or particularly high memory usage\nwithin a single process. With that, I think it's safe to reenable 2\nparallel test workers.",
        "commit_title": "Default to 1 worker process on GraalPy in cythonize (#8143)",
