    "body": "Hi @da-woods, I was looking at the memory usage of tests and found that there are several large spikes due to tests that spawn worker processes. Here's what locally helped me to cut down on peak memory usage:\n- Make `cythonize` use serial builds on GraalPy by default. `ProcessPoolExecutor` creates a process per CPU core, which is excessive on GraalPy. We patch `multiprocessing.Pool` to lower the default number of processes if you pass `None`, but we missed that `ProcessPoolExecutor` has its own code for this so it's still using CPU core count.\n- Reduce the parallelism on GraalPy used by `common_include_dir` test. There other tests that still have parallelism, but those didn't show up in my investigation, so I'm keeping this minimal for now.\n\nI haven't found any memory leaks or particularly high memory usage within a single process. With that, I think it's safe to reenable 2 parallel test workers.",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-16T18:36:54Z",
